<details><summary>What to compare</summary><p>In KoMandir, the accent also supplies focus color, and the primary button uses the workbench background for text. Rachana has separate accent-fill, focus and on-accent values. Its example edits fill only to show those independent roles; an application palette may derive them from one setting. KoMandir MiniPopup uses the panel surface; its default buttons and Dropdown lists use the raised surface. Selection is a separate role.</p><p>Expand “Resolved shared color roles” in either example. Palettes change at the document root so portals inherit the same colors and standard 12 px text. Preview adjustments separate buttons from popup surfaces in light, Shravanam and KoMandir palettes. Rachana dark keeps its source colors. Each popup uses a prepared text field with memory state.</p></details>
<details><summary>Connection and limits</summary><pre><code>{'import "@karatala/ui-theme/rachana.css";\ndocument.documentElement.dataset.karatalaTheme = "rachana";\n\n// Keep the existing application palette and control stylesheet.\n// Shared presentation: color: var(--karatala-color-text);'}</code></pre><p>The CSS adapter is optional and does not choose a palette. The examples use source-derived color snapshots, not application settings. Musical colors, file statuses, disabled opacity, dimensions and focus policy stay with their current owners. The application roots have not yet adopted this alias layer.</p></details>
